NAME
    qemu-test.sh - build, create and launch m-boot QEMU smoke-test images

SYNOPSIS
    tests/qemu-test.sh --target TARGET --output DIR
                       [--scenario loader|recovery|both] [--stage DIR]
                       [--modules-dir DIR] [--grub-mkimage PATH]
                       [--bios-modules-dir DIR]
                       [--firmware-code FILE --firmware-vars FILE]
                       [--prepare-only] [--headless]

DESCRIPTION
    Runs build.sh (unless --stage is supplied) and creates a disposable
    raw GPT image for each requested scenario using tests/qemu-image.sh.
    By default it launches each image interactively via tests/qemu-run.sh.
    When --scenario both is selected (the default), close the loader QEMU
    guest to proceed to the recovery guest. Root is required for virtual
    loop device and filesystem creation; no physical device is modified.
    --prepare-only builds both images without opening a QEMU window.

EXPECTED RESULTS
    loader:   GRUB reaches the externally staged 'm-loader TEST' menu;
              selecting inspection shows root, prefix and devices.
    recovery: GRUB reaches the embedded recovery menu because the external
              /m/boot/loader/init file is absent.
    BIOS:     requires --bios-modules-dir and grub-bios-setup. Unlike the
              production installer, the test embeds BIOS boot sectors only
              into a verified temporary file-backed loop device.

EXAMPLES
    sudo tests/qemu-test.sh --target x86_64-efi --output ./qemu-out
    sudo tests/qemu-test.sh --target arm64-efi --output ./qemu-arm \
      --modules-dir /usr/lib/grub/arm64-efi --prepare-only
    sudo tests/qemu-test.sh --target i386-pc --output ./qemu-bios \
      --bios-modules-dir /usr/lib/grub/i386-pc

LIMITATIONS
    Requires a Linux host with the real GRUB target modules and QEMU tools.
    A QEMU process starting is not proof that firmware boot succeeded;
    inspect both boot scenarios. No physical hardware/USB/Thunderbolt test
    is performed. An existing build stage or image is not overwritten.

